    <a href="#remember">Remember</a>
  </nav>

  <main>
    <section id="overview">
      <h2>Lesson Overview</h2>

      <div class="lesson-info">
        <article class="info-card">
          <strong>Course</strong>
          AI Tools for Developers
        </article>

        <article class="info-card">
          <strong>Lesson</strong>
          Lesson 6
        </article>

        <article class="info-card">
          <strong>Topic</strong>
          Prompt and Context Engineering
        </article>

        <article class="info-card">
          <strong>Level</strong>
          Beginner
        </article>
      </div>

      <h3>Learning Objectives</h3>

      <p>
        By the end of this lesson, you should be able to:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>
          Write prompts that are clear, concise, and precise.
        </li>

        <li>
          Separate useful context from unnecessary information.
        </li>

        <li>
          Think and plan before sending a prompt.
        </li>

        <li>
          Warn the AI about known difficulties and common mistakes.
        </li>

        <li>
          Tell an AI agent which tools or features it should use.
        </li>

        <li>
          Understand that the developer remains responsible
          for directing and reviewing the AI.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <div class="important">
        <strong>Main principle:</strong>
        AI does not remove the developer from the process.
        The developer defines the goal, supplies the right context,
        sets the limits, and checks the result.
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="english">
      <h2>English Technical Section</h2>

      <p>
        Prompt engineering is the practice of writing instructions
        that clearly describe what an AI system should do.
      </p>

      <p>
        Context engineering is the practice of supplying the
        information, files, rules, examples, and constraints that
        the AI needs to perform the task correctly.
      </p>

      <p>
        A strong result normally requires both:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>A clear instruction.</li>
        <li>Relevant supporting information.</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="recommendation-grid">
        <article class="recommendation-card">
          <div class="number">1</div>

          <h3>Be Concise and Precise</h3>

          <p>
            A prompt should contain enough detail to define the task,
            but it should not be filled with unrelated explanations.
          </p>

          <p>
            Concise does not mean incomplete. It means that every
            sentence should help the AI understand the goal.
          </p>

          <h4>A precise prompt usually identifies:</h4>

          <ul>
            <li>The exact task.</li>
            <li>The part of the project involved.</li>
            <li>Important limits.</li>
            <li>The expected output.</li>
            <li>How success should be checked.</li>
          </ul>

          <div class="warning">
            Very long prompts can still be unclear when they contain
            repeated ideas, unnecessary history, or unrelated details.
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="recommendation-card">
          <div class="number">2</div>

          <h3>Avoid Unnecessary Context</h3>

          <p>
            Context is useful only when it helps the AI complete
            the current task.
          </p>

          <p>
            Do not attach or reference a file simply because you
            suspect that it might be related. Include files that you
            know contain relevant code, settings, requirements,
            or examples.
          </p>

          <h4>Useful context may include:</h4>

          <ul>
            <li>The file where the problem occurs.</li>
            <li>A related configuration file.</li>
            <li>The exact error message.</li>
            <li>A required design or business rule.</li>
            <li>An example of the expected result.</li>
          </ul>

          <h4>Unnecessary context may include:</h4>

          <ul>
            <li>Unrelated project files.</li>
            <li>Old instructions that no longer apply.</li>
            <li>Long documentation pages unrelated to the task.</li>
            <li>Personal stories that do not affect the solution.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="recommendation-card">
          <div class="number">3</div>

          <h3>Think, Plan, Then Prompt</h3>

          <p>
            Before sending a request to an AI tool, pause and identify
            what you actually want to achieve.
          </p>

          <p>
            For a larger task, prepare a small plan first. This
            reduces repeated clarification and prevents the AI from
            making broad changes too early.
          </p>

          <ol class="steps">
            <li>
              Define the problem.
            </li>

            <li>
              Identify the files or systems involved.
            </li>

            <li>
              Decide what must not change.
            </li>

            <li>
              Describe the desired final result.
            </li>

            <li>
              Write and review the prompt.
            </li>
          </ol>

          <p>
            Planning mode is especially useful for tasks that involve
            several files, complex logic, unfamiliar code, or
            important data.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="recommendation-card">
          <div class="number">4</div>

          <h3>Do Not Hide Known Challenges</h3>

          <p>
            Do not deliberately withhold information just to see
            whether the AI can discover the problem by itself.
          </p>

          <p>
            When you already know about a dangerous area, common
            mistake, previous failure, or special requirement,
            include that information in the original prompt.
          </p>

          <h4>For example:</h4>

          <pre><code>The registration form previously created duplicate student records.

Keep the existing duplicate-checking logic.
Do not remove or bypass it when adding the new language field.</code></pre>

          <p>
            This gives the AI a better chance of completing the task
            without reintroducing an old problem.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="recommendation-card">
          <div class="number">5</div>

          <h3>Name the Tools the AI Should Use</h3>

          <p>
            AI coding agents may have access to several tools and
            features. These can include terminal commands, search,
            web access, testing tools, project search, connected
            servers, skills, or specialized subagents.
          </p>

          <p>
            When a specific tool is necessary, mention it directly.
            Do not assume the agent will automatically choose it.
          </p>

          <h4>Example:</h4>

          <pre><code>Use the terminal to run the existing test command after the change.

Do not install new packages.

If a test fails, report the exact error before editing another file.</code></pre>

          <p>
            This instruction tells the agent which tool to use,
            what not to do, and how to respond if a problem appears.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="recommendation-card">
          <div class="number">6</div>

          <h3>You Remain in Control</h3>

          <p>
            The AI may suggest code, edit files, run commands,
            analyze errors, or review changes. However, the developer
            remains responsible for the direction of the work.
          </p>

          <p>
            You should decide:
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li>What the AI is allowed to change.</li>
            <li>Which files it may inspect.</li>
            <li>Which tools it should use.</li>
            <li>How the result should be tested.</li>
            <li>Whether the final output is acceptable.</li>
          </ul>

          <div class="success">
            The AI is an assistant. The developer is the decision-maker.
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>

      <h3>Recommended Prompt Structure</h3>

      <p>
        A practical developer prompt can use the following structure:
      </p>

      <pre><code>Task:
Describe exactly what should be done.

Relevant context:
List the files, error message, or rules that matter.

Constraints:
State what must not be changed.

Tools:
Name any tool, command, or feature that should be used.

Verification:
Explain how the result should be checked.

Output:
State what the AI should return after completing the work.</code></pre>

      <h3>Complete Example</h3>

      <pre><code>Task:
Add a required preferred-language field to the student registration page.

Relevant context:
The page is in src/app/register.tsx.
The students table already has a language column.
The choices must be English and Somali.

Constraints:
Keep the existing duplicate-student check.
Do not change payment logic.
Do not edit unrelated files.
Keep the existing page design.

Tools:
Search the project for the existing registration insert function.
Run the existing type-check command after editing.

Verification:
Confirm that registration cannot be submitted without selecting a language.
Confirm that the selected language is saved.

Output:
Return the complete replacement register.tsx file and list the checks performed.</code></pre>

      <p>
        This prompt is detailed, but every part supports the task.
        It does not include unrelated background information.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="somali" class="somali">
      <h2>Qaybta Farsamada ee Af-Soomaaliga</h2>

      <p>
        Prompt engineering waa habka loo qoro amar ama codsi cad
        oo AI-ga u sheegaya waxa la rabo inuu qabto.
      </p>

      <p>
        Context engineering waa habka AI-ga loo siiyo macluumaadka,
        faylasha, xeerarka, tusaalooyinka, iyo xuduudaha muhiimka u ah
        hawsha.
      </p>

      <h3>1. Prompt-ka Ka Dhig Mid Kooban oo Sax ah</h3>

      <p>
        Prompt-ku waa inuu si cad u qeexaa hawsha. Waa inuu leeyahay
        faahfaahinta muhiimka ah, laakiin waa inuusan ku buuxsamin
        hadal aan hawsha waxba ka tarayn.
      </p>

      <p>
        Kooban macnaheedu ma aha in xog muhiim ah laga tago.
        Macnaheedu waa in jumlad kasta ay leedahay sabab ay prompt-ka
        ugu jirto.
      </p>

      <h3>2. Ha Bixin Context Aan Loo Baahnayn</h3>

      <p>
        Context badan mar walba ma fiicna. Context-ka wanaagsan waa
        xogta si toos ah uga caawinaysa AI-ga hawsha hadda taagan.
      </p>

      <p>
        Ha ku darin fayl aad keliya u malaynayso inuu muhiim yahay.
        Ku dar faylasha aad ogtahay inay hayaan code-ka, setting-ka,
        qaladka, ama xeerka la xiriira hawsha.
      </p>

      <h4>Context muhiim ah waxaa ka mid noqon kara:</h4>

      <ul>
        <li>Faylka qaladku ka jiro.</li>
        <li>Qoraalka error-ka oo dhammeystiran.</li>
        <li>Xeer ganacsi oo aan la beddeli karin.</li>
        <li>Tusaale muujinaya natiijada la rabo.</li>
        <li>Configuration si toos ah hawsha ula xiriira.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>3. Fikir, Qorshee, Kadib Prompt Qor</h3>

      <p>
        Ha bilaabin prompt-ka adigoon si cad u garanayn waxa aad
        rabto. Marka hore faham dhibaatada, kadib samee qorshe yar,
        ugu dambaynna qor prompt-ka.
      </p>

      <ol class="steps">
        <li>
          Caddee dhibaatada.
        </li>

        <li>
          Ogaaw faylasha ama nidaamka ay khusayso.
        </li>

        <li>
          Sheeg waxa aan la beddeli karin.
        </li>

        <li>
          Qeex natiijada ugu dambaysa.
        </li>

        <li>
          Dib u akhri prompt-ka ka hor intaadan dirin.
        </li>
      </ol>

      <h3>4. Ha Ka Qarin AI-ga Dhibaatada Aad Hore u Ogtahay</h3>

      <p>
        Haddii aad ogtahay meel adag, khalad hore u dhacay, ama
        dhibaatada caanka ah, AI-ga u sheeg bilowga.
      </p>

      <p>
        Ujeeddadu ma aha in AI-ga la imtixaamo. Ujeeddadu waa in
        hawsha si sax ah loo dhammeeyo.
      </p>

      <pre><code>Foomkani hore ayuu u samayn jiray student isku mid ah laba jeer.

Ha ka saarin duplicate-checking logic-ka.
Markaad field-ka cusub ku darto, hubi in ilaalintaas ay sii shaqaynayso.</code></pre>

      <h3>5. Si Cad U Sheeg Tool-ka La Isticmaalayo</h3>

      <p>
        Coding agent-ku wuxuu heli karaa tools kala duwan sida
        terminal, search, tests, web, skills, ama adeegyo kale.
      </p>

      <p>
        Haddii tool gaar ah loo baahan yahay, magaca tool-ka ku qor
        prompt-ka. Ha sugin in AI-gu si otomaatig ah u doorto.
      </p>

      <pre><code>Isticmaal terminal-ka si aad u orodsiiso test-ka jira.

Ha rakibin package cusub.

Haddii test-ku fashilmo, marka hore ii sheeg error-ka saxda ah.</code></pre>

      <h3>6. Adiga Ayaa Maamula AI-ga</h3>

      <p>
        AI-gu wuu soo jeedin karaa code, wax buu beddeli karaa,
        commands ayuu orodsiin karaa, ama errors ayuu baari karaa.
        Laakiin developer-ka ayaa masuul ka ah jihada hawsha.
      </p>

      <p>
        Adiga ayaa go'aaminaya:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>Waxa AI-ga loo oggol yahay inuu beddelo.</li>
        <li>Faylasha uu arki karo.</li>
        <li>Tools-ka uu isticmaali karo.</li>
        <li>Sida natiijada loo tijaabinayo.</li>
        <li>In shaqada la aqbalayo iyo in kale.</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="important">
        <strong>Fikradda ugu muhiimsan:</strong>
        AI-gu waa kaaliye. Adiga ayaa hagaya, xaddidaya,
        hubinaya, oo leh go'aanka ugu dambeeya.
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="comparison">
      <h2>Weak and Improved Prompt Examples</h2>

      <div class="example-grid">
        <article class="example-card bad">
          <span class="label label-bad">
            Weak Prompt
          </span>

          <h3>Example 1</h3>

          <pre><code>Fix my page.</code></pre>

          <p>
            This prompt does not identify the page, the problem,
            the expected behavior, or the limits.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="example-card good">
          <span class="label label-good">
            Improved Prompt
          </span>

          <h3>Example 1</h3>

          <pre><code>Inspect src/app/index.tsx.

The Register button does not open the registration route.

Find the cause and fix only that navigation problem.
Do not redesign the page.
Return the complete replacement index.tsx file.</code></pre>
        </article>

        <article class="example-card bad">
          <span class="label label-bad">
            Weak Prompt
          </span>

          <h3>Example 2</h3>

          <pre><code>Look at all my files and improve everything.</code></pre>

          <p>
            This request has no clear boundary and may cause many
            unwanted changes.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="example-card good">
          <span class="label label-good">
            Improved Prompt
          </span>

          <h3>Example 2</h3>

          <pre><code>Review only the registration form validation.

Check that name, email, phone, and preferred language are required.

Do not change the page design or database structure.
List any validation problem before editing.</code></pre>
        </article>

        <article class="example-card bad">
          <span class="label label-bad">
            Weak Prompt
          </span>

          <h3>Example 3</h3>

          <pre><code>Add a feature. You should know what I mean.</code></pre>

          <p>
            The AI cannot reliably infer the intended feature,
            location, rules, or output.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="example-card good">
          <span class="label label-good">
            Improved Prompt
          </span>

          <h3>Example 3</h3>

          <pre><code>Add a Back to Home button to the bottom of the learner portal.

Use Expo Router.
The button should open "/".
Keep all existing learner data and login logic unchanged.</code></pre>
        </article>
      </div>

      <h3>Prompt Quality Checklist</h3>

      <div class="table-wrapper">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Question</th>
              <th>Why It Matters</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>

          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>
                Did I clearly state the task?
              </td>

              <td>
                The AI needs a specific objective.
              </td>
            </tr>

            <tr>
              <td>
                Did I include only relevant context?
              </td>

              <td>
                Unrelated information may distract the AI.
              </td>
            </tr>

            <tr>
              <td>
                Did I name the correct files?
              </td>

              <td>
                This reduces unnecessary project-wide searching.
              </td>
            </tr>

            <tr>
              <td>
                Did I state what must not change?
              </td>

              <td>
                Clear limits protect working features.
              </td>
            </tr>

            <tr>
              <td>
                Did I mention known risks?
              </td>

              <td>
                The AI can avoid repeating known mistakes.
              </td>
            </tr>

            <tr>
              <td>
                Did I name required tools?
              </td>

              <td>
                The AI should not have to guess which tool to use.
              </td>
            </tr>

            <tr>
              <td>
                Did I define verification?
              </td>

              <td>
                Testing helps confirm that the result works.
              </td>
            </tr>

            <tr>
              <td>
                Did I define the output format?
              </td>

              <td>
                The AI can return code, a plan, a report,
                or another requested format correctly.
              </td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="gal-english" class="gal">
      <h2>GAL — English Analogy</h2>

      <h3>Giving Directions to a Driver</h3>

      <p>
        Imagine that you hire a driver to take a package to a
        particular building.
      </p>

      <p>
        A weak instruction would be:
      </p>

      <pre><code>Take this somewhere downtown.</code></pre>

      <p>
        The driver does not know the exact building, route,
        deadline, contact person, or delivery rules.
      </p>

      <p>
        A stronger instruction would be:
      </p>

      <pre><code>Deliver this package to the blue office building on Main Street.

Use the front entrance.
Ask for Fatima at reception.
Do not leave the package outside.
Call me if the office is closed.</code></pre>

      <p>
        This instruction gives the goal, relevant context,
        restrictions, and a response plan for a possible problem.
      </p>

      <div class="important">
        Prompt engineering works the same way. The AI performs better
        when the destination, limits, known risks, and expected result
        are clearly explained.
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="gal-somali" class="gal somali">
      <h2>GAL — Tusaalaha Af-Soomaaliga</h2>

      <h3>Darawal Loo Dhiibayo Alaab</h3>

      <p>
        Ka fikir inaad darawal siisay alaab uu geeyo meel gaar ah.
      </p>

      <p>
        Amar aan fiicnayn wuxuu noqon karaa:
      </p>

      <pre><code>Alaabtan meel magaalada dhexdeeda ah gee.</code></pre>

      <p>
        Darawalku ma garanayo dhismaha, waddada, qofka qaadanaya,
        waqtiga, ama waxa uu samaynayo haddii meesha la xiro.
      </p>

      <p>
        Amar cad wuxuu noqon karaa:
      </p>

      <pre><code>Alaabtan gee dhismaha buluugga ah ee Main Street.

Ka gal albaabka hore.
Reception-ka ka weydii Fatima.
Alaabta bannaanka ha uga tegin.
Haddii xafiisku xiran yahay, i soo wac.</code></pre>

      <p>
        Amarkani wuxuu leeyahay ujeeddo cad, context muhiim ah,
        xuduud, iyo waxa la samaynayo haddii dhibaato timaaddo.
      </p>

      <div class="success">
        Sida darawalka loo hago ayaa AI-gana loo hagaa.
        Prompt cad wuxuu yareeyaa qaladka iyo shaqada dib loogu noqdo.
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="html-tags">
      <h2>HTML Elements Used in This Lesson</h2>

      <p>
        This lesson uses semantic HTML elements to organize
        recommendations, examples, tables, activities, and answers.
      </p>

      <div class="table-wrapper">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Element</th>
              <th>Opening Tag</th>
              <th>Closing Tag</th>
              <th>Common Attributes</th>
              <th>Browser Purpose</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>

          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>Header</td>
              <td><code>&lt;header&gt;</code></td>
              <td><code>&lt;/header&gt;</code></td>
              <td><code>id</code>, <code>class</code></td>
              <td>
                Displays the lesson introduction and title.
              </td>
            </tr>

            <tr>
              <td>Navigation</td>
              <td><code>&lt;nav&gt;</code></td>
              <td><code>&lt;/nav&gt;</code></td>
              <td>
                <code>aria-label</code>,
                <code>class</code>
              </td>
              <td>
                Contains links to lesson sections.
              </td>
            </tr>

            <tr>
              <td>Section</td>
              <td><code>&lt;section&gt;</code></td>
              <td><code>&lt;/section&gt;</code></td>
              <td><code>id</code>, <code>class</code></td>
              <td>
                Groups related lesson content.
              </td>
            </tr>

            <tr>
              <td>Article</td>
              <td><code>&lt;article&gt;</code></td>
              <td><code>&lt;/article&gt;</code></td>
              <td><code>class</code>, <code>id</code></td>
              <td>
                Creates a self-contained recommendation or example.
              </td>
            </tr>

            <tr>
              <td>Ordered List</td>
              <td><code>&lt;ol&gt;</code></td>
              <td><code>&lt;/ol&gt;</code></td>
              <td><code>class</code>, <code>start</code></td>
              <td>
                Displays steps in a numbered order.
              </td>
            </tr>

            <tr>
              <td>Preformatted Text</td>
              <td><code>&lt;pre&gt;</code></td>
              <td><code>&lt;/pre&gt;</code></td>
              <td><code>class</code></td>
              <td>
                Preserves spacing and line breaks in prompt examples.
              </td>
            </tr>

            <tr>
              <td>Code</td>
              <td><code>&lt;code&gt;</code></td>
              <td><code>&lt;/code&gt;</code></td>
              <td><code>class</code></td>
              <td>
                Identifies code, commands, or technical text.
              </td>
            </tr>

            <tr>
              <td>Details</td>
              <td><code>&lt;details&gt;</code></td>
              <td><code>&lt;/details&gt;</code></td>
              <td><code>open</code>, <code>class</code></td>
              <td>
                Creates expandable content.
              </td>
            </tr>

            <tr>
              <td>Summary</td>
              <td><code>&lt;summary&gt;</code></td>
              <td><code>&lt;/summary&gt;</code></td>
              <td><code>class</code></td>
              <td>
                Creates the clickable heading for details content.
              </td>
            </tr>

            <tr>
              <td>Footer</td>
              <td><code>&lt;footer&gt;</code></td>
              <td><code>&lt;/footer&gt;</code></td>
              <td><code>id</code>, <code>class</code></td>
              <td>
                Displays information at the bottom of the page.
              </td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h3>Example: Ordered List</h3>

      <pre><code>&lt;ol&gt;
  &lt;li&gt;Think about the problem.&lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;li&gt;Make a plan.&lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;li&gt;Write the prompt.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;</code></pre>

      <div class="browser-output">
        <h4>Browser Output</h4>

        <ol>
          <li>Think about the problem.</li>
          <li>Make a plan.</li>
          <li>Write the prompt.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>

      <h3>Example: Details and Summary</h3>

      <pre><code>&lt;details&gt;
  &lt;summary&gt;Show the improved prompt&lt;/summary&gt;

  &lt;p&gt;
    Fix only the Register button navigation.
  &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/details&gt;</code></pre>

      <div class="browser-output">
        <h4>Browser Output</h4>

        <details>
          <summary>Show the improved prompt</summary>

          <p>
            Fix only the Register button navigation.
          </p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="practice">
      <h2>Practical Activity</h2>

      <h3>Activity 1: Remove Unnecessary Context</h3>

      <div class="activity-card">
        <p>
          Read the prompt below:
        </p>

        <pre><code>I started learning computers many years ago.
My favorite color is blue.
Yesterday I spoke to my friend.
My project has many files.
Please fix the Register button in src/app/index.tsx.
It should open /register.
Do not redesign the page.</code></pre>

        <p>
          Which sentences are important to the task?
        </p>

        <details>
          <summary>Show suggested answer</summary>

          <p class="answer">
            Keep only the information about the file, the button,
            the correct route, and the design restriction.
          </p>

          <pre><code>Fix the Register button in src/app/index.tsx.

It should open /register.
Do not redesign the page.</code></pre>
        </details>
      </div>

      <h3>Activity 2: Improve a Weak Prompt</h3>

      <div class="activity-card">
        <p>
          Weak prompt:
        </p>

        <pre><code>Make registration better.</code></pre>

        <p>
          Rewrite it by adding:
        </p>

        <ul>
          <li>The exact task.</li>
          <li>The relevant file.</li>
          <li>What must not change.</li>
          <li>How the result should be checked.</li>
        </ul>

        <details>
          <summary>Show one possible answer</summary>

          <pre><code>Add a required preferred-language field to src/app/register.tsx.

The choices must be English and Somali.

Keep the existing student ID generation and duplicate-checking logic.
Do not change payment-related code.

Verify that the form cannot submit without a language selection.
Return the complete replacement register.tsx file.</code></pre>
        </details>
      </div>

      <h3>Activity 3: Identify the Missing Information</h3>

      <div class="activity-card">
        <p>
          Prompt:
        </p>

        <pre><code>Run the tests after fixing the page.</code></pre>

        <p>
          What may still be missing?
        </p>

        <details>
          <summary>Show suggested answer</summary>

          <ul>
            <li>The page or file that needs fixing.</li>
            <li>The exact problem.</li>
            <li>The test command.</li>
            <li>The expected behavior.</li>
            <li>What to do if a test fails.</li>
          </ul>
        </details>
      </div>

      <h3>Activity 4: Think, Plan, Prompt</h3>

      <div class="activity-card">
        <p>
          Before asking an AI agent to add a new certificate page,
          complete this planning form:
        </p>

        <ol>
          <li>
            What should the certificate page display?
          </li>

          <li>
            Which student conditions unlock the certificate?
          </li>

          <li>
            Which files are likely involved?
          </li>

          <li>
            What existing logic must remain unchanged?
          </li>

          <li>
            How will you verify that the page works?
          </li>
        </ol>

        <div class="important">
          Do not send the prompt until these questions have clear answers.
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="quiz">
      <h2>Multiple-Choice Quiz</h2>

      <div class="question">
        <p>
          1. What is the main goal of prompt engineering?
        </p>

        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q1" />
          A. To make every prompt extremely long
        </label>

        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q1" />
          B. To give the AI clear and useful instructions
        </label>

        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q1" />
          C. To hide the task from the AI
        </label>

        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q1" />
          D. To avoid checking the result
        </label>
      </div>

      <div class="question">
        <p>
          2. What is useful context?
        </p>

        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q2" />
          A. Any available information
        </label>

        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q2" />
          B. Information that directly helps with the task
        </label>

        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q2" />
          C. Personal stories unrelated to the project
        </label>

        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q2" />
          D. Every file in the computer
        </label>
      </div>

      <div class="question">
        <p>
          3. What should you do before writing a prompt for
          a complex task?
        </p>

        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q3" />
          A. Think about the problem and make a plan
        </label>

        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q3" />
          B. Ask the AI to change everything
        </label>

        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q3" />
          C. Hide all known information
        </label>

        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q3" />
          D. Delete the project
        </label>
      </div>

      <div class="question">
        <p>
          4. If you know about a common mistake, what should you do?
        </p>

        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q4" />
          A. Hide it and test whether the AI fails
        </label>

        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q4" />
          B. Include it in the prompt with guidance
        </label>

        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q4" />
          C. Mention it only after the project breaks
        </label>

        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q4" />
          D. Ignore it completely
        </label>
      </div>

      <div class="question">
        <p>
          5. Why should you name a required tool in the prompt?
        </p>

        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q5" />
          A. So the AI does not have to guess which tool to use
        </label>

        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q5" />
          B. So the prompt becomes confusing
        </label>

        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q5" />
          C. Because tools never affect the task
        </label>

        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q5" />
          D. To prevent all testing
        </label>
      </div>

      <div class="question">
        <p>
          6. Which prompt is more precise?
        </p>

        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q6" />
          A. Fix everything
        </label>

        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q6" />
          B. Improve my app somehow
        </label>

        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q6" />
          C. Fix only the Register button navigation in index.tsx
        </label>

        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q6" />
          D. Do whatever you think
        </label>
      </div>

      <div class="question">
        <p>
          7. Who controls the direction of AI-assisted development?
        </p>

        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q7" />
          A. The responsible developer
        </label>

        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q7" />
          B. Nobody
        </label>

        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q7" />
          C. The keyboard
        </label>

        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q7" />
          D. The browser window
        </label>
      </div>

      <div class="question">
        <p>
          8. What should a verification instruction explain?
        </p>

        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q8" />
          A. How to confirm that the result works
        </label>

        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q8" />
          B. How to avoid all tests
        </label>

        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q8" />
          C. How to add unrelated files
        </label>

        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="q8" />
          D. How to make the prompt longer
        </label>
      </div>

      <details>
        <summary>Open Answer Key</summary>

        <ol>
          <li>
            <strong>B</strong> — Give the AI clear instructions.
          </li>

          <li>
            <strong>B</strong> — Information directly supporting the task.
          </li>

          <li>
            <strong>A</strong> — Think and plan first.
          </li>

          <li>
            <strong>B</strong> — Include the known problem and guidance.
          </li>

          <li>
            <strong>A</strong> — Avoid making the AI guess.
          </li>

          <li>
            <strong>C</strong> — It identifies the exact file and task.
          </li>

          <li>
            <strong>A</strong> — The responsible developer remains in control.
          </li>

          <li>
            <strong>A</strong> — Explain how to confirm the result works.
          </li>
        </ol>
      </details>
    </section>

    <section id="remember" class="remember">
      <h2>Remember</h2>

      <ul>
        <li>
          A good prompt is clear, focused, and specific.
        </li>

        <li>
          Include enough detail to define the task, but remove
          information that does not help.
        </li>

        <li>
          Provide files and documentation only when they are relevant.
        </li>

        <li>
          Think first, make a plan, and then write the prompt.
        </li>

        <li>
          Tell the AI about known risks, previous failures,
          and common mistakes.
        </li>

        <li>
          Name the tools, commands, or features that should be used.
        </li>

        <li>
          State what must not change.
        </li>

        <li>
          Explain how the final work should be verified.
        </li>

        <li>
          The AI assists, but the developer remains responsible.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Somali Remember</h3>

      <ul>
        <li>
          Prompt wanaagsan waa mid cad, kooban, oo sax ah.
        </li>

        <li>
          Ku dar context-ka muhiimka ah oo keliya.
        </li>

        <li>
          Marka hore fikir, kadib qorshee, ugu dambayn prompt qor.
        </li>

        <li>
          AI-ga u sheeg khataraha iyo khaladaadka aad hore u ogtahay.
        </li>

        <li>
          Si cad u sheeg tool-ka ama command-ka la isticmaalayo.
        </li>

        <li>
          Sheeg waxa aan la beddeli karin.
        </li>

        <li>
          Sheeg sida natiijada loo hubinayo.
        </li>

        <li>
          AI-gu waa kaaliye; developer-ka ayaa maamula.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>
